{
  "requirement": "Saving encodes the completed result using its Serde JSON representation and\npreserves the dependencies captured in `Fingerprinted`.\n`Record`, `Dependency`, and `Fingerprint` support\nSerde when their type parameters do. The graph's node\nidentities and edge labels need not implement Serde unless its storage backend\nrequires those bounds.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Record<N, L = ()> {\n    pub version: Option<CriterionVersion>,\n    pub dependencies: Vec<Dependency<N, L>>,\n    pub output: Value,\n}\n\nimpl<N, L> Record<N, L> {\n    pub fn new(\n        version: Option<CriterionVersion>,\n        dependencies: Vec<Dependency<N, L>>,\n        output: Value,\n    ) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<N: Clone, L: Clone> Clone for Record<N, L>;\nimpl<N: Debug, L: Debug> Debug for Record<N, L>;\nimpl<'de, N, L> Deserialize<'de> for Record<N, L> where N: Deserialize<'de>, L: Deserialize<'de>;\nimpl<N, L> Serialize for Record<N, L> where N: Serialize, L: Serialize;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the marked tests adequately cover `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record`. I found no gap.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that cover them**\n\n1. **Saving encodes the completed result as Serde JSON.**\n   - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` stores a record and then asserts the saved `Record.output` equals `json!({\"satisfied\":false,\"details\":[...]})`.\n   - The same test asserts the saved output is `json!(null)` for a unit-typed answer.\n   - It also asserts that `verify` alone writes nothing (`writes == 0`).\n\n2. **Saving preserves the dependencies captured in `Fingerprinted`.**\n   - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations]` saves a review that reads `Node(2)`. It asserts the stored `dependencies` equal `[Dependency::Node(Node(2), Fingerprint::new(\"text-v1\",\"after\"))]`.\n   - The first test also asserts that records saved without reads have empty dependencies.\n\n3. **`Record`, `Dependency` and `Fingerprint` support Serde when their type parameters do.**\n   - `tests/storage.rs#fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]` stores and loads a `Record<String, ()>`. It asserts `version`, `dependencies` and `output` are unchanged.\n   - Its `record` helper covers both `Dependency::Node` and `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`, each with a `Fingerprint`.\n   - The same test round-trips a `Record<String, String>` with a non-unit edge label (`\"tests/é\"`) and asserts the version, dependencies and output survive.\n   - It asserts that loading with an incompatible `N` (`u8`) or `L` (`u8`) gives `FileStorageError::Json`. That shows the Serde bounds are real.\n   - Malformed JSON is also reported as an error.\n\n4. **Node identities and edge labels need not implement Serde.**\n   - The contracts tests keep `Record<Node, _>` in the in-memory `Application` domain through `store_evidence` and `load_evidence`. They do this without any JSON encoding of `Node`.\n   - Storage tests use `String` identities and labels, which do implement Serde.\n   - The text says \"need not … unless its storage backend requires\", so it does not demand a separate negative test.\n\n5. **Shape of the type.**\n   - `Record::new` and the public fields are used by the integration tests, which sit outside the crate. `storage.rs#fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]` calls `Record::new` and reads `.version`, `.dependencies` and `.output`.\n   - `#[non_exhaustive]` is consistent with those tests, which only use `Record::new`.\n   - The `Clone` impl is exercised through `record.clone()` in the in-memory `store_evidence` and `load_evidence` helpers. The marked contracts tests reach those helpers.\n   - `Debug`, `Clone`, `Serialize` and `Deserialize` come from a single `#[derive]` on `struct[Record]` in `src/graph.rs`. That code has no conditional logic of its own, so it qualifies for the exemption. The tests cover it anyway.\n   - `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the exported inventory.\n\n**Marking.** `tests/storage.rs#fn[record_preserves_the_stored_version_encoding]` also tests the Serde representation of `Record`. It does not carry a `{test}` reference to this requirement. Other marked tests already cover the requirement, so I did not treat this as a gap.\n\n**Unmet obligations, acknowledgments:** none and none.",
